{"subjectId":"java","id":"file-io","title":"File I/O with java.nio.file","group":"Functional Java & Standard Library","order":56,"html":"<p class=\"lead\">Modern file handling uses <code>Path</code> and the static helpers in <code>Files</code> — one line for small files, buffered streams for large ones, try-with-resources for everything that must be closed.</p>\n<section class=\"block\"><h3><i class=\"ti ti-history\"></i>The two generations</h3>\n<div class=\"table-wrap\"><table><thead><tr><th></th><th><code>java.io</code> (1996)</th><th><code>java.nio.file</code> (Java 7, NIO.2)</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Path type</td><td><code>File</code></td><td><code>Path</code> (<code>Path.of(\"a\", \"b.txt\")</code>)</td></tr><tr><td>Errors</td><td>many methods return <code>false</code> silently</td><td>descriptive <code>IOException</code>s (<code>NoSuchFileException</code>…)</td></tr><tr><td>Helpers</td><td>streams and readers only</td><td><code>Files.readString</code>, <code>write</code>, <code>lines</code>, <code>walk</code>, <code>copy</code>, <code>move</code>…</td></tr><tr><td>Extras</td><td>—</td><td>symbolic links, attributes, <code>WatchService</code>, file systems (zip)</td></tr></tbody></table></div>\n<p>Streams (<code>InputStream</code>/<code>OutputStream</code>) move <strong>bytes</strong>; readers/writers (<code>Reader</code>/<code>Writer</code>) move <strong>characters</strong> and need a charset. Always name it (<code>StandardCharsets.UTF_8</code>) — the <code>Files</code> methods default to UTF-8.</p>\n</section><section class=\"block\"><h3><i class=\"ti ti-route\"></i><code>Path</code> basics</h3>\n<figure data-lang=\"java\" class=\"code\"><figcaption>Java</figcaption><pre><code>import java.nio.file.*;\n\npublic class Main {\n    public static void main(String[] args) {\n        Path p = Path.of(\"/home/asha/docs/../notes/report.txt\");\n        System.out.println(p.getFileName());\n        System.out.println(p.getParent());\n        System.out.println(p.normalize());\n        System.out.println(p.getNameCount());\n        System.out.println(Path.of(\"/data\").resolve(\"logs/app.log\"));\n        System.out.println(Path.of(\"/a/b\").relativize(Path.of(\"/a/c/d\")));\n        System.out.println(p.toString().endsWith(\".txt\"));\n    }\n}</code></pre></figure><figure data-lang=\"text\" class=\"code\"><figcaption>Output</figcaption><pre><code>report.txt\n/home/asha/docs/../notes\n/home/asha/notes/report.txt\n6\n/data/logs/app.log\n../c/d\ntrue</code></pre></figure>\n</section><section class=\"block\"><h3><i class=\"ti ti-file\"></i>Small files: one-liners</h3>\n<figure data-lang=\"java\" class=\"code\"><figcaption>Java</figcaption><pre><code>import java.io.IOException;\nimport java.nio.file.*;\nimport java.util.*;\n\npublic class Main {\n    public static void main(String[] args) throws IOException {\n        Path file = Files.createTempFile(\"notes\", \".txt\");\n        try {\n            Files.writeString(file, \"line one\\nline two\\n\");\n            Files.write(file, List.of(\"line three\"), StandardOpenOption.APPEND);\n\n            System.out.print(Files.readString(file));\n            List&lt;String&gt; lines = Files.readAllLines(file);\n            System.out.println(lines.size() + \" lines, last = \" + lines.get(lines.size() - 1));\n            System.out.println(Files.exists(file) + \" \" + Files.size(file) + \" bytes\");\n        } finally {\n            Files.deleteIfExists(file);\n        }\n        System.out.println(\"exists after delete: \" + Files.exists(file));\n    }\n}</code></pre></figure><figure data-lang=\"text\" class=\"code\"><figcaption>Output</figcaption><pre><code>line one\nline two\nline three\n3 lines, last = line three\ntrue 29 bytes\nexists after delete: false</code></pre></figure>\n<div class=\"callout callout--warn\"><div class=\"callout-label\">Watch out</div><p><code>readString</code> / <code>readAllLines</code> load the <strong>whole file</strong> into memory — fine for configs, an <code>OutOfMemoryError</code> for a 5 GB log. Stream large files instead.</p></div>\n</section><section class=\"block\"><h3><i class=\"ti ti-arrows-down\"></i>Large files: stream line by line</h3>\n<figure data-lang=\"java\" class=\"code\"><figcaption>Java</figcaption><pre><code>import java.io.*;\nimport java.nio.charset.StandardCharsets;\nimport java.nio.file.*;\nimport java.util.stream.*;\n\npublic class Main {\n    public static void main(String[] args) throws IOException {\n        Path log = Files.createTempFile(\"app\", \".log\");\n        try {\n            try (BufferedWriter w = Files.newBufferedWriter(log, StandardCharsets.UTF_8)) {\n                for (int i = 1; i &lt;= 5; i++) {\n                    w.write((i % 2 == 0 ? \"ERROR \" : \"INFO \") + \"event \" + i);\n                    w.newLine();\n                }\n            }                                           // closed (and flushed) here\n\n            try (BufferedReader r = Files.newBufferedReader(log)) {\n                String line;\n                while ((line = r.readLine()) != null) {\n                    if (line.startsWith(\"ERROR\")) System.out.println(line);\n                }\n            }\n\n            try (Stream&lt;String&gt; lines = Files.lines(log)) {   // lazy — must be closed\n                System.out.println(lines.filter(l -&gt; l.startsWith(\"INFO\")).count() + \" info lines\");\n            }\n        } finally {\n            Files.delete(log);\n        }\n    }\n}</code></pre></figure><figure data-lang=\"text\" class=\"code\"><figcaption>Output</figcaption><pre><code>ERROR event 2\nERROR event 4\n3 info lines</code></pre></figure>\n<div class=\"callout callout--note\"><div class=\"callout-label\">Close what you open</div><p><code>Files.lines</code>, <code>Files.list</code>, <code>Files.walk</code> and <code>Files.newBufferedReader</code> hold an open file handle. Wrap them in <strong>try-with-resources</strong>, or you leak file descriptors until the GC gets around to it.</p></div>\n</section><section class=\"block\"><h3><i class=\"ti ti-folders\"></i>Directories: create, walk, copy, move</h3>\n<figure data-lang=\"java\" class=\"code\"><figcaption>Java</figcaption><pre><code>import java.io.IOException;\nimport java.nio.file.*;\nimport java.util.*;\nimport java.util.stream.*;\n\npublic class Main {\n    public static void main(String[] args) throws IOException {\n        Path root = Files.createTempDirectory(\"demo\");\n        Files.createDirectories(root.resolve(\"src/main\"));\n        Files.writeString(root.resolve(\"src/main/App.java\"), \"class App {}\");\n        Files.writeString(root.resolve(\"README.md\"), \"# demo\");\n        Files.copy(root.resolve(\"README.md\"), root.resolve(\"src/README.copy\"));\n        Files.move(root.resolve(\"README.md\"), root.resolve(\"NOTES.md\"));\n\n        try (Stream&lt;Path&gt; all = Files.walk(root)) {\n            all.map(p -&gt; root.relativize(p).toString().replace('\\\\', '/'))\n               .filter(s -&gt; !s.isEmpty())\n               .sorted()\n               .forEach(System.out::println);\n        }\n\n        try (Stream&lt;Path&gt; all = Files.walk(root)) {       // delete children before parents\n            for (Path p : all.sorted(Comparator.reverseOrder()).toList()) Files.delete(p);\n        }\n        System.out.println(Files.exists(root));\n    }\n}</code></pre></figure><figure data-lang=\"text\" class=\"code\"><figcaption>Output</figcaption><pre><code>NOTES.md\nsrc\nsrc/README.copy\nsrc/main\nsrc/main/App.java\nfalse</code></pre></figure>\n<div class=\"table-wrap\"><table><thead><tr><th>Task</th><th>Call</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Create dir (and parents)</td><td><code>Files.createDirectories(path)</code></td></tr><tr><td>List one level / whole tree</td><td><code>Files.list(dir)</code> / <code>Files.walk(dir)</code> / <code>Files.find(dir, depth, matcher)</code></td></tr><tr><td>Copy / move (overwrite)</td><td><code>Files.copy(a, b, StandardCopyOption.REPLACE_EXISTING)</code> / <code>Files.move(...)</code></td></tr><tr><td>Delete</td><td><code>Files.delete(p)</code> (throws if missing) / <code>Files.deleteIfExists(p)</code></td></tr><tr><td>Checks</td><td><code>Files.exists</code>, <code>isDirectory</code>, <code>isRegularFile</code>, <code>isReadable</code>, <code>size</code>, <code>getLastModifiedTime</code></td></tr><tr><td>Binary</td><td><code>Files.readAllBytes</code>, <code>Files.newInputStream</code> / <code>newOutputStream</code></td></tr></tbody></table></div>\n<details class=\"qa\"><summary>Why wrap I/O in try-with-resources?</summary><div><p>Files, sockets and streams hold OS resources. try-with-resources calls <code>close()</code> automatically in reverse order, even when an exception is thrown, and records exceptions from <code>close()</code> as <em>suppressed</em> instead of losing the original one. Before Java 7 this took a verbose <code>finally</code> block that was easy to get wrong.</p></div></details>\n<details class=\"qa\"><summary>Why use BufferedReader/BufferedWriter?</summary><div><p>Unbuffered streams make a system call for every read/write. Buffering batches data in an in-memory buffer (8 KB by default), cutting system calls dramatically; <code>BufferedReader</code> also adds <code>readLine()</code>. Remember that a <code>BufferedWriter</code> must be flushed/closed or the last chunk never reaches the file.</p></div></details>\n<details class=\"qa\"><summary>Byte streams vs character streams?</summary><div><p><code>InputStream</code>/<code>OutputStream</code> handle raw bytes — images, zip files, serialized objects. <code>Reader</code>/<code>Writer</code> handle text and decode/encode it with a charset. Bridge them with <code>InputStreamReader</code> / <code>OutputStreamWriter</code>, always passing an explicit charset.</p></div></details></section>"}